WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:05.078
The next day Holmes was in a good mood when he showed up at my room before breakfast.

2
00:00:05.079 --> 00:00:09.878
"I've been awake since six o'clock and already put in two hours of work!" he announced.

3
00:00:09.879 --> 00:00:14.937
I finished tying my tie and put on my waistcoat. "I can tell that you've solved the case."

4
00:00:14.938 --> 00:00:20.121
"An excellent observation, my dear Watson. Look at this!" Holmes held out his hand.

5
00:00:20.122 --> 00:00:24.488
On his palm were three lumps of black clay speckled with something like sawdust.

6
00:00:24.489 --> 00:00:26.688
"You had only two lumps yesterday."

7
00:00:26.689 --> 00:00:31.388
"I added another one today, and I'm sure all three came from the same place."

8
00:00:31.389 --> 00:00:35.448
Holmes put the clay in his pocket. "Can you survive without breakfast?

9
00:00:35.449 --> 00:00:39.326
I'd like to go to St. Luke's College and put Soames out of his misery."

10
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.512
When we arrived, Soames was so agitated that he could hardly stand still.

11
00:00:44.513 --> 00:00:48.742
"Thank goodness you're here!" Soames mopped his brow with a handkerchief.

12
00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:50.867
"Can the exam proceed as usual?"

13
00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:53.657
"Yes, go ahead," Holmes replied.

14
00:00:53.658 --> 00:00:56.055
"But what about the scoundrel who tried to cheat?"

15
00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:58.454
"Don't worry about him," Holmes said.

16
00:00:58.455 --> 00:01:02.005
"I know who he is, and he won't be competing for the scholarship.

17
00:01:02.006 --> 00:01:04.827
Now, let's arrange your chairs before we confront him."

18
00:01:04.828 --> 00:01:08.097
Holmes pulled three chairs into a row and took the middle one.

19
00:01:08.098 --> 00:01:13.080
Motioning for us to sit beside him, he glanced from side to side with a satisfied smile.

20
00:01:13.081 --> 00:01:17.304
"We look intimidating enough to strike fear into the heart of any guilty person.

21
00:01:17.304 --> 00:01:20.404
Soames, please ring the bell and summon your servant."

22
00:01:21.265 --> 00:01:25.344
When Bannister entered the room, he shrank back in surprise and fear.

23
00:01:25.345 --> 00:01:30.365
"Now, Bannister," Holmes said, "please tell us the truth about yesterday's incident."

24
00:01:30.366 --> 00:01:34.277
Bannister turned pale. "I've told you everything, sir."

25
00:01:34.278 --> 00:01:39.203
"Then let me make a suggestion. You pretended to be ill and sat down on the desk chair.

26
00:01:39.204 --> 00:01:44.064
Why? Because you wanted to conceal something that would identify whoever had been in the room."

27
00:01:44.065 --> 00:01:46.821
"Certainly not!" Bannister snapped.

28
00:01:46.822 --> 00:01:52.722
Holmes pressed on. "The moment Mr. Soames left the room, you released the person who was hiding in the bedroom."

29
00:01:52.723 --> 00:01:56.441
"There was no person, sir." Bannister looked defiant.

30
00:01:56.442 --> 00:01:59.662
"Ah, that's a pity because now I know that you've lied."

31
00:01:59.663 --> 00:02:03.017
"There was no person, sir," Bannister repeated.

32
00:02:03.018 --> 00:02:06.395
Holmes frowned as Bannister stubbornly refused to cooperate.

33
00:02:06.952 --> 00:02:09.856
Then he asked Soames to fetch Gilchrist.

34
00:02:09.857 --> 00:02:14.037
When they returned, the student looked cheerful—until he spotted Bannister.

35
00:02:14.038 --> 00:02:18.693
"Mr. Gilchrist, what led you to cheat on the exam?" Holmes asked.

36
00:02:18.694 --> 00:02:22.908
The horrified young man staggered and cast a reproachful look at Bannister.

37
00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:26.815
"I never said a word, Mr. Gilchrist!" Bannister protested.

38
00:02:26.816 --> 00:02:32.691
"But now, Bannister, you have said something incriminating, so I know you were involved," Holmes said.

39
00:02:32.692 --> 00:02:36.551
"As for you, young man, your only hope lies in a full confession."

40
00:02:36.552 --> 00:02:39.094
Gilchrist fell on his knees before Holmes.

41
00:02:39.095 --> 00:02:42.340
Burying his face in his hands, he burst into sobs.

42
00:02:42.341 --> 00:02:47.365
"We know you're not a hard-core criminal." Holmes patted him gently on the shoulder.

43
00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.922
"Perhaps it would be easier if I describe what happened.

44
00:02:49.923 --> 00:02:52.717
You can correct me if I get anything wrong."

45
00:02:53.544 --> 00:02:55.041
Gilchrist nodded.

46
00:02:55.042 --> 00:03:00.619
"When we were in the courtyard last evening," Holmes began, "I looked through Mr. Soames' window.

47
00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.242
I wondered how tall a man must be to see any papers on the desk.

48
00:03:04.243 --> 00:03:08.074
I'm six feet tall, and I could do it only by standing on my tiptoes.

49
00:03:08.075 --> 00:03:10.719
So the culprit had to be taller than I am."

50
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.227
"I'm six feet, three inches," Gilchrist whispered.

51
00:03:14.228 --> 00:03:19.568
"Another clue was that you compete in the long jump, a track-and-field event that requires spiked shoes."

52
00:03:19.569 --> 00:03:21.268
Gilchrist nodded again.

53
00:03:21.269 --> 00:03:27.194
According to the great detective, Gilchrist had spent the afternoon on the athletic fields, practicing his jumps.

54
00:03:27.195 --> 00:03:30.108
He returned to the courtyard, carrying his jumping shoes.

55
00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:36.037
As he passed Soames' window, he saw some papers on the desk and wondered if they were the exam proofs.

56
00:03:36.974 --> 00:03:41.828
Gilchrist probably would have just continued on his way to his room, but then he noticed something.

57
00:03:41.829 --> 00:03:43.389
The key was in the door.

58
00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:48.023
"On a whim you decided to enter and see if the papers were indeed the proofs," Holmes said.

59
00:03:48.024 --> 00:03:50.198
"There was no risk involved at this point.

60
00:03:50.199 --> 00:03:54.253
If you got caught, you could simply say you'd popped in to ask a question.

61
00:03:54.254 --> 00:03:58.282
But when you realized you'd found the proofs, you couldn't resist the temptation.

62
00:03:58.283 --> 00:04:02.275
You put your shoes down on the desktop, but what did you drop on the desk chair?"

63
00:04:02.276 --> 00:04:04.955
"My gloves," Gilchrist said weakly.

64
00:04:04.956 --> 00:04:08.589
"Aha!" Holmes clapped, startling the poor student.

65
00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:15.319
"One at a time, you took the proofs to the table by the window, so that you could keep an eye out for Soames' return.

66
00:04:15.702 --> 00:04:20.336
When you heard him at the door, you grabbed your shoes, and the spikes cut the leather desktop.

67
00:04:20.337 --> 00:04:23.828
But as you ran for the bedroom, you forgot your gloves."

68
00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:31.400
"That explains the cut," I said, "but what do the black pieces of clay have to do with anything? And the sawdust?"

69
00:04:31.401 --> 00:04:33.643
Holmes removed the clay from his pocket.

70
00:04:33.644 --> 00:04:37.364
He had suspected that the clay had been clinging to the shoe spikes.

71
00:04:37.365 --> 00:04:43.131
So this morning he walked over to the athletic fields, where he discovered that black clay was used in the jump pit.

72
00:04:43.393 --> 00:04:47.410
"Sawdust is sprinkled over the clay to prevent the athletes from slipping."

73
00:04:47.411 --> 00:04:51.601
Holmes stared at the student. "Is my story correct, Mr. Gilchrist?"

74
00:04:51.602 --> 00:04:56.089
"Yes, sir." Gilchrist stood up and took a deep breath.

75
00:04:56.668 --> 00:04:58.789
Soames appeared to be shocked.

76
00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.243
"That's all you have to say, Mr. Gilchrist?"

77
00:05:01.244 --> 00:05:04.986
Gilchrist pulled a paper from his pocket and handed it to Soames.

78
00:05:04.987 --> 00:05:09.387
"I felt so guilty about cheating, I was up all night, writing you this letter.

79
00:05:09.388 --> 00:05:12.129
Read it and you'll see I'm withdrawing from the college."

80
00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:16.812
Soames looked surprised. "What made you change your mind about the scholarship?"

81
00:05:16.813 --> 00:05:18.701
Gilchrist pointed at Bannister.

82
00:05:18.702 --> 00:05:21.181
"This man persuaded me to do the right thing."

83
00:05:21.182 --> 00:05:24.136
Holmes turned to Bannister with a quizzical expression.

84
00:05:24.137 --> 00:05:28.298
"For many years I was a butler for Mr. Gilchrist's father," Bannister said.

85
00:05:28.299 --> 00:05:32.538
"When he died, I came here to work, but I never forgot my old employer.

86
00:05:32.539 --> 00:05:36.167
Out of loyalty to the father, I watched over the son."

87
00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:42.749
Bannister explained that when he came into the room yesterday, he noticed Gilchrist's gloves on the desk chair.

88
00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:47.832
"They're an unusual color, and if Mr. Soames saw them, he'd know they were Mr. Gilchrist's."

89
00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:52.582
So the faithful servant sat on the gloves and refused to budge until Soames went for Holmes.

90
00:05:52.583 --> 00:05:56.004
Then Gilchrist came out of the bedroom and confessed to Bannister.

91
00:05:56.005 --> 00:06:00.039
"It was my duty to speak to him as his father would have done," Bannister said.

92
00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.589
"I told him that he couldn't profit from cheating."

93
00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.525
"No, indeed." Holmes sprang to his feet.

94
00:06:05.526 --> 00:06:07.433
"I wish you good luck, young man.

95
00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:12.254
You may have fallen, but let's hope you learn from this experience and rise to new heights."

96
00:06:12.255 --> 00:06:19.428
He turned to me. "And now, Watson, I think we've earned some breakfast!"

